{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NLNZG2a6gsZuYqbGs1cPtZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Full CKA Analysis: MVP Models\n2\t\n3\t**Date**: 2026-05-21\n4\t**Script**: `compute_cka.py` (Linear CKA, Kornblith et al. 2019)\n5\t**Data**: 14,042 parallel samples per language pair, MMLU domains\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct (mvp_001)\n10\t\n11\t### Full CKA Matrix (en → target)\n12\t\n13\t| Layer | zh | ar | hi | sw | ko | **Mean** |\n14\t|-------|------|------|------|------|------|----------|\n15\t| 0 | 0.912 | 0.901 | 0.536 | 0.440 | 0.687 | **0.695** |\n16\t| 4 | 0.652 | 0.642 | 0.519 | 0.470 | 0.630 | **0.583** |\n17\t| 8 | 0.815 | 0.737 | 0.593 | 0.604 | 0.724 | **0.695** |\n18\t| 12 | 0.843 | 0.820 | 0.614 | 0.612 | 0.789 | **0.735** |\n19\t| 16 | 0.886 | 0.883 | 0.575 | 0.593 | 0.865 | **0.760** |\n20\t| 20 | 0.764 | 0.664 | 0.371 | 0.399 | 0.670 | **0.574** |\n21\t| 24 | 0.694 | 0.544 | 0.162 | 0.125 | 0.551 | **0.415** |\n22\t| 27 | 0.345 | 0.356 | 0.117 | 0.084 | 0.318 | **0.244** |\n23\t| **Mean** | **0.739** | **0.693** | **0.436** | **0.416** | **0.654** | |\n24\t\n25\t### Depth Profile\n26\t- Peak similarity at **layer 16** (mean CKA = 0.760)\n27\t- Sharp decline after layer 16: 0.760 → 0.574 → 0.415 → 0.244\n28\t- Layer 0→4 dip (0.695 → 0.583) then recovery through mid-layers\n29\t\n30\t---\n31\t\n32\t## 2. Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct (mvp_003)\n33\t\n34\t### Full CKA Matrix (en → target)\n35\t\n36\t| Layer | zh | ar | hi | sw | ko | **Mean** |\n37\t|-------|------|------|------|------|------|----------|\n38\t| 0 | 0.881 | 0.678 | 0.198 | 0.265 | 0.767 | **0.558** |\n39\t| 4 | 0.930 | 0.924 | 0.531 | 0.712 | 0.910 | **0.801** |\n40\t| 8 | 0.891 | 0.880 | 0.553 | 0.746 | 0.879 | **0.790** |\n41\t| 12 | 0.922 | 0.905 | 0.624 | 0.705 | 0.893 | **0.810** |\n42\t| 16 | 0.857 | 0.830 | 0.511 | 0.671 | 0.841 | **0.742** |\n43\t| 20 | 0.636 | 0.568 | 0.350 | 0.387 | 0.575 | **0.503** |\n44\t| 24 | 0.607 | 0.527 | 0.275 | 0.300 | 0.542 | **0.450** |\n45\t| 28 | 0.581 | 0.482 | 0.221 | 0.256 | 0.503 | **0.409** |\n46\t| 31 | 0.469 | 0.306 | 0.162 | 0.266 | 0.382 | **0.317** |\n47\t| **Mean** | **0.753** | **0.678** | **0.381** | **0.479** | **0.699** | |\n48\t\n49\t### Depth Profile\n50\t- Peak similarity at **layer 12** (mean CKA = 0.810)\n51\t- Layer 0 notably low (0.558) due to hi/sw tokenizer divergence at embedding layer\n52\t- Decline onset earlier than Qwen: layer 12→16 already drops 0.810→0.742\n53\t\n54\t---\n55\t\n56\t## 3. Cross-Model Comparison\n57\t\n58\t### Per-Layer Mean CKA\n59\t\n60\t| Depth (relative) | Qwen Layer | Qwen CKA | Llama Layer | Llama CKA |\n61\t|-------------------|------------|-----------|-------------|-----------|\n62\t| 0% | 0 | 0.695 | 0 | 0.558 |\n63\t| ~15% | 4 | 0.583 | 4 | 0.801 |\n64\t| ~30% | 8 | 0.695 | 8 | 0.790 |\n65\t| ~45% | 12 | 0.735 | 12 | 0.810 |\n66\t| ~60% | 16 | 0.760 | 16 | 0.742 |\n67\t| ~75% | 20 | 0.574 | 20 | 0.503 |\n68\t| ~85% | 24 | 0.415 | 24 | 0.450 |\n69\t| ~95% | 27 | 0.244 | 28 | 0.409 |\n70\t| 100% | — | — | 31 | 0.317 |\n71\t\n72\t### Key Patterns\n73\t\n74\t1. **Both models show monotonic CKA decline in upper layers** (layer 16/12 onward), confirming language-specific divergence deepens toward output.\n75\t\n76\t2. **Qwen peaks later (layer 16) vs Llama (layer 12)**: Qwen maintains higher cross-lingual alignment deeper into the network.\n77\t\n78\t3. **Qwen's final-layer CKA is lower** (0.244 at L27) **than Llama's** (0.317 at L31), despite Qwen having fewer layers — suggesting Qwen's representations diverge more sharply at the output.\n79\t\n80\t4. **Language ranking is consistent across models**: zh > ar/ko > sw > hi (with ko and ar swapping in some layers).\n81\t\n82\t5. **Llama layer 0 anomaly**: CKA at layer 0 is much lower for Llama (0.558) vs Qwen (0.695), driven by hi (0.198) and sw (0.265). This likely reflects tokenizer-level divergence at the embedding layer.\n83\t\n84\t### Per-Language Mean CKA Comparison\n85\t\n86\t| Language | Qwen | Llama | Delta |\n87\t|----------|------|-------|-------|\n88\t| zh | 0.739 | 0.753 | +0.014 |\n89\t| ar | 0.693 | 0.678 | −0.016 |\n90\t| ko | 0.654 | 0.699 | +0.045 |\n91\t| hi | 0.436 | 0.381 | −0.055 |\n92\t| sw | 0.416 | 0.479 | +0.063 |\n93\t\n94\t---\n95\t\n96\t## 4. Comparison with Prior cka_vs_degradation Analysis\n97\t\n98\tPrior analysis (from registry) established correlations between CKA and calibration transfer degradation:\n99\t\n100\t| Metric | Qwen | Llama |\n101\t|--------|------|-------|\n102\t| Spearman(CKA, degradation) | ρ=−0.309, p=0.053 | ρ=−0.519, p=0.001 |\n103\t| Interpretation | Marginal trend | Significant negative correlation |\n104\t\n105\t**Consistency check**: The full CKA run here matches the prior per-language means exactly (zh=0.739, ar=0.693, etc.), confirming data integrity.\n106\t\n107\t**Key insight**: The stronger CKA–degradation correlation in Llama aligns with Llama's sharper layer-0 anomaly and earlier CKA peak — suggesting Llama's cross-lingual representations are more heterogeneous across the depth axis, making layer selection for calibration transfer more critical.\n108\t\n109\t---\n110\t\n111\t## 5. CSV File Locations\n112\t\n113\t- Qwen2.5-7B: `westd-13176:/root/xling_calib_direction/results_cka_mvp001/cka_matrix_qwen25_7b.csv`\n114\t- Llama-3.1-8B: `westd-13176:/root/xling_calib_direction/results_cka_mvp003/cka_matrix_llama31_8b.csv`\n115\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3bed0805-e277-4cba-a173-e5dbb10b2135","uuid":"4f0691fa-8610-429e-b09c-5d0459c2102b","timestamp":"2026-05-21T04:58:07.607Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/artifacts/cka_mvp_full_results.md","content":"# Full CKA Analysis: MVP Models\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-21\n**Script**: `compute_cka.py` (Linear CKA, Kornblith et al. 2019)\n**Data**: 14,042 parallel samples per language pair, MMLU domains\n\n---\n\n## 1. Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct (mvp_001)\n\n### Full CKA Matrix (en → target)\n\n| Layer | zh | ar | hi | sw | ko | **Mean** |\n|-------|------|------|------|------|------|----------|\n| 0 | 0.912 | 0.901 | 0.536 | 0.440 | 0.687 | **0.695** |\n| 4 | 0.652 | 0.642 | 0.519 | 0.470 | 0.630 | **0.583** |\n| 8 | 0.815 | 0.737 | 0.593 | 0.604 | 0.724 | **0.695** |\n| 12 | 0.843 | 0.820 | 0.614 | 0.612 | 0.789 | **0.735** |\n| 16 | 0.886 | 0.883 | 0.575 | 0.593 | 0.865 | **0.760** |\n| 20 | 0.764 | 0.664 | 0.371 | 0.399 | 0.670 | **0.574** |\n| 24 | 0.694 | 0.544 | 0.162 | 0.125 | 0.551 | **0.415** |\n| 27 | 0.345 | 0.356 | 0.117 | 0.084 | 0.318 | **0.244** |\n| **Mean** | **0.739** | **0.693** | **0.436** | **0.416** | **0.654** | |\n\n### Depth Profile\n- Peak similarity at **layer 16** (mean CKA = 0.760)\n- Sharp decline after layer 16: 0.760 → 0.574 → 0.415 → 0.244\n- Layer 0→4 dip (0.695 → 0.583) then recovery through mid-layers\n\n---\n\n## 2. Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct (mvp_003)\n\n### Full CKA Matrix (en → target)\n\n| Layer | zh | ar | hi | sw | ko | **Mean** |\n|-------|------|------|------|------|------|----------|\n| 0 | 0.881 | 0.678 | 0.198 | 0.265 | 0.767 | **0.558** |\n| 4 | 0.930 | 0.924 | 0.531 | 0.712 | 0.910 | **0.801** |\n| 8 | 0.891 | 0.880 | 0.553 | 0.746 | 0.879 | **0.790** |\n| 12 | 0.922 | 0.905 | 0.624 | 0.705 | 0.893 | **0.810** |\n| 16 | 0.857 | 0.830 | 0.511 | 0.671 | 0.841 | **0.742** |\n| 20 | 0.636 | 0.568 | 0.350 | 0.387 | 0.575 | **0.503** |\n| 24 | 0.607 | 0.527 | 0.275 | 0.300 | 0.542 | **0.450** |\n| 28 | 0.581 | 0.482 | 0.221 | 0.256 | 0.503 | **0.409** |\n| 31 | 0.469 | 0.306 | 0.162 | 0.266 | 0.382 | **0.317** |\n| **Mean** | **0.753** | **0.678** | **0.381** | **0.479** | **0.699** | |\n\n### Depth Profile\n- Peak similarity at **layer 12** (mean CKA = 0.810)\n- Layer 0 notably low (0.558) due to hi/sw tokenizer divergence at embedding layer\n- Decline onset earlier than Qwen: layer 12→16 already drops 0.810→0.742\n\n---\n\n## 3. Cross-Model Comparison\n\n### Per-Layer Mean CKA\n\n| Depth (relative) | Qwen Layer | Qwen CKA | Llama Layer | Llama CKA |\n|-------------------|------------|-----------|-------------|-----------|\n| 0% | 0 | 0.695 | 0 | 0.558 |\n| ~15% | 4 | 0.583 | 4 | 0.801 |\n| ~30% | 8 | 0.695 | 8 | 0.790 |\n| ~45% | 12 | 0.735 | 12 | 0.810 |\n| ~60% | 16 | 0.760 | 16 | 0.742 |\n| ~75% | 20 | 0.574 | 20 | 0.503 |\n| ~85% | 24 | 0.415 | 24 | 0.450 |\n| ~95% | 27 | 0.244 | 28 | 0.409 |\n| 100% | — | — | 31 | 0.317 |\n\n### Key Patterns\n\n1. **Both models show monotonic CKA decline in upper layers** (layer 16/12 onward), confirming language-specific divergence deepens toward output.\n\n2. **Qwen peaks later (layer 16) vs Llama (layer 12)**: Qwen maintains higher cross-lingual alignment deeper into the network.\n\n3. **Qwen's final-layer CKA is lower** (0.244 at L27) **than Llama's** (0.317 at L31), despite Qwen having fewer layers — suggesting Qwen's representations diverge more sharply at the output.\n\n4. **Language ranking is consistent across models**: zh > ar/ko > sw > hi (with ko and ar swapping in some layers).\n\n5. **Llama layer 0 anomaly**: CKA at layer 0 is much lower for Llama (0.558) vs Qwen (0.695), driven by hi (0.198) and sw (0.265). This likely reflects tokenizer-level divergence at the embedding layer.\n\n### Per-Language Mean CKA Comparison\n\n| Language | Qwen | Llama | Delta |\n|----------|------|-------|-------|\n| zh | 0.739 | 0.753 | +0.014 |\n| ar | 0.693 | 0.678 | −0.016 |\n| ko | 0.654 | 0.699 | +0.045 |\n| hi | 0.436 | 0.381 | −0.055 |\n| sw | 0.416 | 0.479 | +0.063 |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Comparison with Prior cka_vs_degradation Analysis\n\nPrior analysis (from registry) established correlations between CKA and calibration transfer degradation:\n\n| Metric | Qwen | Llama |\n|--------|------|-------|\n| Spearman(CKA, degradation) | ρ=−0.309, p=0.053 | ρ=−0.519, p=0.001 |\n| Interpretation | Marginal trend | Significant negative correlation |\n\n**Consistency check**: The full CKA run here matches the prior per-language means exactly (zh=0.739, ar=0.693, etc.), confirming data integrity.\n\n**Key insight**: The stronger CKA–degradation correlation in Llama aligns with Llama's sharper layer-0 anomaly and earlier CKA peak — suggesting Llama's cross-lingual representations are more heterogeneous across the depth axis, making layer selection for calibration transfer more critical.\n\n---\n\n## 5. CSV File Locations\n\n- Qwen2.5-7B: `westd-13176:/root/xling_calib_direction/results_cka_mvp001/cka_matrix_qwen25_7b.csv`\n- Llama-3.1-8B: `westd-13176:/root/xling_calib_direction/results_cka_mvp003/cka_matrix_llama31_8b.csv`\n","numLines":115,"startLine":1,"totalLines":115}}}
